# lychee ignore patterns (regex)
#
# IndyKite API and MCP server base URLs. The bare root `/` of each is
# documented in manifests/descriptions as the per-region base URL, but the
# actual API only serves sub-paths (e.g. /configs/v1/..., /contx-iq/v1/...).
# Lychee gets a 404 on the bare host and flags it — it's not a broken link,
# it's just an unhealth-checkable base hostname.
^https://(eu|us)\.api\.indykite\.com/?$
^https://(eu|us)\.mcp\.indykite\.com/?$
^https://(eu|us)\.token-service\.indykite\.com/?$

# Docker-internal hostname placeholders used as examples in the gateway and
# Intent Agent templates, scripts and manifests (lychee checks YAML, shell
# and JSON files as plain text, unlike markdown code spans). They are
# documentation, not real links — lychee can't resolve service names from
# outside the deployment's network, and localhost is the documented default
# of a self-hosted service.
^http://(orchestrator|retriever|weather|chatbot|intent|mcp-server|token-service)(:[0-9]+)?(/.*)?$
^http://localhost(:[0-9]+)?(/.*)?$
^http://127\.0\.0\.1(:[0-9]+)?(/.*)?$
